# In the paraxial equation a tilted beam advances sideways by z sin(angle), not z tan(angle): 3.49 against 3.49 um here.
# Reference: z sin(angle), the paraxial result.
title Gaussian beam tilted by 2 degrees
grid dx=0.05 dz=0.125
window width=80 length=100
launch gaussian x=0 radius=3 tilt=2
plane end z=100
expect total end 1.000000000 2e-7
expect centroid end 3.4893811 2e-6
expect radius end 11.7754812 2e-6
expect neff 1.442469491 2e-8
expect centroid end 3.48995 0.02
expect radius end 11.77769 0.04
